WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.969
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 5, Network troubleshooting, which is 24 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.969 --> 00:00:10.585
This lesson covers objective 5 point 3.

00:00:10.585 --> 00:00:15.078
Given a scenario, troubleshoot common issues with network services.

00:00:15.078 --> 00:00:16.822
Here's a classic scenario.

00:00:16.822 --> 00:00:19.840
The device has an address, but nothing works.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.906
Three PCs on one switch.

00:00:23.906 --> 00:00:25.860
A and B work together fine.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.200
PC C got an address by D H C P, but it can't reach its neighbors.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:35.000
Notice its port sits in a different VLAN, so it landed on a different network.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:39.623
The port's VLAN decides the subnet, and the subnet decides who you can reach.

00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:42.020
So check the VLAN on the switch port first.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.580
Move the port into the right VLAN and the problem goes away.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:55.420
When a device gets a DHCP address but can't talk to neighbors that work fine, check the V LAN assigned to its switch port first.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.410
That's objective five point three.
